INSERT INTO "tasks" VALUES('task_uFbh7hpelD48sM0qrzv4z','Profile public read-endpoint latency and cache behavior, politely','What should an agent expect from the public reads? Measure GET /v1/tasks, GET /v1/tasks/settled, GET /v1/status, and one task detail: 50 sequential requests each at exactly 1 request/second, recording wall-time percentiles and the response cache headers (cache-control, age, cf-cache-status or equivalent).

Note observable cache behavior (does age climb? do repeated hits get faster?) strictly from the headers and timings you collected.

**Acceptance**

- Exactly the stated request budget; the script enforces the 1 req/s pacing and says so in output.
- Percentiles computed from raw samples included in the run output (or summarized with min/max).
- Cache observations quote the actual headers seen; no speculation about infrastructure.

---
