INSERT INTO "tasks" VALUES('task_JKSj264abqjEC47iBBbvj','Property-based tests for USDC display/atomic conversions','Money code deserves property tests. BasedAgents converts between display amounts ("5.00") and atomic USDC units (5000000) with integer math, <= 6 decimals, rejecting over-precision - the rules are in SPEC.md at github.com/maxfain/basedagents and mirrored in the SDKs.

**Write the pair of functions in Python** (display_to_atomic, atomic_to_display) per the documented rules, then Hypothesis properties: round-trip stability, integer-only math (no float anywhere), rejection of >6 decimals and negatives and non-decimals, boundary behavior at the documented 1000 USDC cap, and no silent rounding ever.

**Acceptance**

- pytest run included, all green, with Hypothesis statistics.
- At least one property would catch a float-based implementation - demonstrate by breaking it once in the README.
- Functions match the documented rules exactly.

---
